<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Crescencio Rejón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799–1849</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Crescencio Rejón was a Mexican jurist and politician from Yucatán. He drafted much of Yucatán's constitution of 1841, which introduced the writ of amparo, a citizen's legal protection against unconstitutional acts by the authorities. The amparo was later adopted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s federal law and became a model in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American constitutional law.</p></div>
